{"status":"unsupported_domain","reason":"A faithful executable contract for all frozen obligations cannot be expressed by the supplied typed AST frontend.","gaps":[{"obligations":["O1","E1","O5"],"description":"The actual result is either JSON null or a list of two-element integer lists. The supplied sort grammar has no nullable-list or union sort, and no specified mapping from Unit or Except to this exact JSON result. Replacing null with an error constructor or a record would change the required output structure."},{"obligations":["S1"],"description":"The supplied term and formula grammar cannot constrain Python imports, external I/O, printing, file or network access, or state retained across calls. A theorem about a pure mathematical function would not establish these implementation requirements."}],"preserved_requirements":{"input":"One JSON object with integer n from 0 through 10 and edges containing directed pairs [u,v].","assumption":"A1 requires conforming caller inputs and must have a satisfiability witness in any complete proposal.","output":"Return null exactly when a directed cycle exists anywhere, including self-loops and disconnected components. Otherwise return unique original edges with no alternate path of at least two edges, ordered lexicographically by source and destination. Ignore duplicate input edges, preserve all reachability, include no redundant edges, and leave isolated vertices implicit.","implementation":"Expose pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) in solution.py, return JSON-serializable values, use only the standard library, perform no external I/O, and retain no state across calls."},"required_extension":"Provide an executable nullable-list sort with explicit JSON null serialization and corresponding branch semantics, plus registered implementation checks for S1. An opaque Lean proposal cannot satisfy the requested strict Python TESTED boundary."}